{
 "id": "DW-10",
 "system": "ac3",
 "sessionId": "bm-ac2-dw-10-f5fecf9058",
 "endReason": "escalated",
 "customerTurns": 5,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "dishwasher wont come on"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is control relay / PCB (last). Check the dishwasher's plug is fully in and its socket or the switched spur (often a switch above the worktop) is on, and try another appliance in that socket. If the electrics have tripped, don't keep resetting it. Was a switch, plug or fuse off (and is it sorted), or does the socket work fine with something else?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Other sockets and lights all work. The switch above the worktop is on and its little light is lit. Nothing tripped at the fuse box either."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is the door latch / door switch. Open the door, check nothing in the racks or the cutlery basket sticks out, then shut it firmly until it clicks and press start. Does it still show the door as open?\n[Safety panel] An appliance that keeps tripping your electrics — or that smells of burning or has scorch marks — may have an electrical fault. Stop using it, switch it off and unplug it, don't keep resetting it, and have it checked by a qualified electrician or appliance engineer."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Door's shut firmly, it clicks fine. Still totally dead, no lights or display at all so it's not showing anything."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is the dishwasher's mains input or control board. Many dishwashers have a child or control lock (often a key or padlock symbol) that stops the buttons working — the manual shows which buttons to hold to turn it off. Was the child / control lock on (and is it off now), or was it already off?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "There's no display at all so I don't think it's a child lock. Nothing lights up whatsoever. What else can I check?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Check if the dishwasher is plugged in securely behind the unit, as a loose connection can cause a total power loss. If it is hardwired into the electrical system, verify that the dedicated circuit breaker for the appliance has not tripped. Next: Note whether moving or pressing the door changes anything. Let me know what you find."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I can't pull the dishwasher out to see behind it, it's integrated. Pressing or moving the door changes nothing, it's still completely dead. Anything else I can try?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Since the power supply and main switch are confirmed working, the issue likely lies with a failed control board or internal wiring. You should contact a qualified appliance repair technician to diagnose the electrical fault safely. A delay start (often shown as a countdown like \"3h\") or a programme that hasn't been confirmed can look like it won't start. Was a delay start set or the programme not selected (and is it sorted), or was nothing like that set?"
  }
 ],
